course: dictionary
lesson: 14062
title: Mastication: chewing food
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Mastication is a formal, science word for chewing. When you chew, your teeth crush food into small bits so it can be swallowed and digested.
explain: «Mastication breaks food into small pieces.» The clue is in the words around it: breaks and small pieces. Try swapping in chewing: «Chewing breaks food into small pieces.» It still makes sense, so chewing is the meaning.
explain: In science lessons you will meet mastication in the phrase «the muscles of mastication». Outside school, people simply say chewing.
fact: Mastication means chewing: crushing food with the teeth.
fact: Mastication is the first stage of digestion, and it happens in the mouth.
fact: Saliva is mixed with food during mastication, which helps digestion begin.
fact: «Mastication» is a formal word; everyday people say «chewing».
fact: The muscles of mastication move your jaw up and down when you chew.
exercise: «Mastication breaks food into small pieces so it can be swallowed.» What does mastication mean? | Drinking water with a meal | Cooking food in a hot pan | Swallowing food whole | *Chewing food with the teeth
exercise: Ella says, «I'll just say chewing.» Which science word means the same as chewing? | *Mastication | Swallowing | Digestion | Saliva
exercise: «The muscles of mastication move your jaw up and down.» Which part of the body is mainly used in mastication? | Ears | Eyes | *Teeth and jaw | Knees
test: Mastication is the first stage of what? | Sleeping | Reading | Breathing | *Digestion
test: Which everyday word is closest in meaning to mastication? | Sneezing | Running | *Chewing | Whispering
exam: Which sentence uses mastication correctly? | *Mastication breaks food into small pieces before we swallow it. | I ran to school with mastication. | Mastication is a bright blue colour. | The soup was mastication.
